---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import Capture from '../components/Capture.astro';
import Architecture from '../components/Architecture.astro';
import Gallery from '../components/Gallery.astro';
import Setup from '../components/Setup.astro';
import coding from '../assets/coding.png';
import status from '../assets/status.png';
import download from '../data/downloads.json';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const github = 'https://github.com/sumitahmed/FreeCompute';
---
<Page>
  <section class="hero container" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow hero-eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line" aria-hidden="true"></span> FreeCompute / v{download.version} beta</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">More compute.<br /><span>Same workspace.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-description">Run open-weight models on remote or local GPU workers. Your files, approvals, sessions and commands stay under your control.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="#setup">Set up FreeCompute <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
          <a class="text-link" href={github}>View on GitHub <Icon name="external" /></a>
        </div>
        <ul class="hero-metadata" aria-label="Product summary"><li>CLI-first</li><li>Local authority</li><li>Apache 2.0</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-proof">
        <Capture image={coding} eager variant="hero" sizes="1200px" label="CLI capture / generated code" alt="Actual FreeCompute CLI returning Java prime-number code through the configured Kaggle Qwen worker." caption="Code returned by a connected Kaggle worker. A detail view of the real CLI; enlarge to see the complete capture." />
        <p class="proof-source"><span>YOUR TERMINAL. YOUR PROJECT.</span><span>Actual capture / 04 Oct 2026</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-bottom"><span>Open-weight models. A local workflow.</span><a href="#inside">See it in use <Icon name="arrow" /></a></div>
  </section>

  <section id="why" class="section why container" aria-labelledby="why-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="section-index">01</span> Why FreeCompute</p>
      <h2 id="why-title">The model can run elsewhere.<br /><span>Your workflow stays here.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="why-copy">
      <p>A capable model can need more VRAM than your PC has. FreeCompute connects a GPU inference worker to the project already on your machine.</p>
      <p>Work in your terminal. Let the model propose the next step. Keep the authority to read, change and run things in the local Core.</p>
      <dl class="local-principles">
        <div><dt><span aria-hidden="true">01</span> Your project</dt><dd>Local file tools and workspace boundaries.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><span aria-hidden="true">02</span> Your approval</dt><dd>Review edits and commands before execution.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><span aria-hidden="true">03</span> Your history</dt><dd>Sessions, task journals and undo stay local.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Gallery />
  <Architecture />

  <section id="compute" class="section container" aria-labelledby="compute-title">
    <div class="section-split">
      <SectionHeading index="04" label="Compute options" title="Bring the compute that fits." id="compute-title" />
      <p class="section-aside">Use the documented Kaggle worker, or configure a compatible endpoint. Hardware, model size and runtime allocation determine what you can run.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="compute-options">
      <article class="compute-option">
        <div class="compute-name"><span class="mono">01 / DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Kaggle</h3><p>Remote notebook</p></div>
        <p>The current notebook targets two Tesla T4 GPUs and a pinned Qwen GGUF profile. Use the fresh worker URL printed by your session.</p>
        <div><p>Keep the notebook running. GPU availability and quota depend on your account.</p><a class="text-link" href={base + 'guide/#worker'}>Notebook setup <Icon name="arrow" /></a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="compute-option">
        <div class="compute-name"><span class="mono">02 / MANUAL</span><h3>Google Colab</h3><p>Bring a compatible worker</p></div>
        <p>Configure a matching inference endpoint and model profile yourself. There is no maintained Colab deployment notebook in this repository.</p>
        <div><p>Hardware and session availability depend on your runtime and plan.</p><a class="text-link" href={base + 'guide/#connect'}>Connection requirements <Icon name="arrow" /></a></div>
      </article>
      <article class="compute-option">
        <div class="compute-name"><span class="mono">03 / CONFIGURABLE</span><h3>Local or private GPU</h3><p>Your own hardware</p></div>
        <p>Point a configured worker profile at a compatible engine endpoint. Choose a model that fits the hardware you provide.</p>
        <div><p>You operate the inference service and its authentication.</p><a class="text-link" href={base + 'guide/#connect'}>Connection guide <Icon name="arrow" /></a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="provider-note">FreeCompute supplies the harness. Your provider supplies the compute, with its own limits and availability.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="models" class="section models container" aria-labelledby="models-title">
    <div class="model-copy">
      <SectionHeading index="05" label="Models & workers" title="Open weights. Configured routes." id="models-title">
        <p>Choose a model and worker profile that fit your task. These captures show the repository’s Qwen 27B GGUF configuration.</p>
      </SectionHeading>
      <dl class="model-support">
        <div><dt>llama.cpp / GGUF</dt><dd>Text and coding with a compatible model profile.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>OpenAI-style endpoints</dt><dd>A configurable text adapter; endpoint capabilities still matter.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>ComfyUI / images</dt><dd>A separate route with the existing fixed Qwen GGUF workflow. Live image deployment remains unverified.</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="model-note">Model families are not a blanket compatibility promise. Files, templates, tool calling and available memory must match the worker.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="model-proof">
      <p class="eyebrow">/status — observed, configured, unknown</p>
      <Capture image={status} variant="status" sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 40px), (max-width: 1320px) 60vw, 710px" label="Worker status" alt="Actual FreeCompute status: a healthy Kaggle worker, two observed Tesla T4 GPUs with VRAM usage, and unknown session limits, CPU, RAM and weekly quota." caption="Two Tesla T4 GPUs observed in this session. CPU, RAM, provider quota and session limits remain explicitly unknown." />
      <p class="model-observation">Hardware readings are observations. Declared context capacity is not full-input certification.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="security" class="section security container" aria-labelledby="security-title">
    <div class="security-layout">
      <div>
        <SectionHeading index="06" label="Security & trust" title="Local by default. Clear about the boundaries." id="security-title">
          <p>Use HTTPS or a private secure transport for remote inference. Know what stays on your machine and what reaches the model.</p>
        </SectionHeading>
        <a class="text-link" href={base + 'guide/#safety'}>Read the safety notes <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
      </div>
      <dl class="security-list">
        <div><dt><Icon name="lock" /> Encrypted in transit</dt><dd>HTTPS protects the connection. Prompts, selected file contents and tool results still reach the inference host.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><Icon name="folder" /> Local authority</dt><dd>File tools, commands, approvals and journals run on your PC. The inference worker has no direct local filesystem or terminal endpoint.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><Icon name="shield" /> Explicit approval</dt><dd>Edits, writes, commands and undo require approval. Approved commands use your host privileges; they are not in an OS sandbox.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Setup />
  <div class="built-with container"><span class="eyebrow">Built on</span><ul aria-label="FreeCompute technologies"><li>Python</li><li>prompt_toolkit</li><li>Rich</li><li>llama.cpp</li><li>SQLite</li></ul><span class="mono">Local Core / Remote inference</span></div>

  <dialog id="capture-dialog" aria-labelledby="capture-dialog-title">
    <div class="dialog-heading"><h2 id="capture-dialog-title">Actual CLI screenshot</h2><button type="button" data-dialog-close autofocus aria-label="Close screenshot"><Icon name="close" /></button></div>
    <div class="dialog-image" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Full-size screenshot; scroll to inspect"><img alt="Actual FreeCompute CLI screenshot" /></div>
    <p data-dialog-caption></p>
  </dialog>
  <script>import '../scripts/interactions';</script>
</Page>
